spans.s:
नीप a. situated low, deep. —m. N. of a tree, n. its blossom
& fruit;
 m. pl. N. of a princely race.

निपातन n. letting fall, throwing down, killing,
destroying;
 occasional mention or use of a word (g.);
 falling or flying
down, descent.

निपात m. fall, ruin, loss, death;
 falling down from (abl.)
into or upon (—˚), flying down, descending;
 falling against, assault,
onset;
 accidental occurrence or mention, exception, irregularity,
particle (g.).

निपातिन् a. falling or flying down;
 descending upon (—˚);
felling, destroying (—˚).

निपुण a. clever, skilful;
 versed in, familiar with (loc.,
*gen., *instr., infin., or —˚);
 exact, complete, perfect. ˚— & n.
adv.;
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.
